Say whether the sound plays to headphones in the audio device modules

Patch 0018 lets AEC3's transparent mode decide sooner that a capture without any sign of
echo has none while the sound plays to headphones or a headset (PlayoutToHeadphones, in
api/audio/audio_device.h), and nothing set it. The audio device modules now set it from
what the system says of the device the playout plays on, and set it false when playout
stops: with no playout there is no sound to headphones. The ALSA module and the macOS
engine device leave it false.

- PulseAudio (Linux): when the playout stream is connected and ready (a start of
  playout), when the server moves it to another sink (the moved callback of patch 0011),
  and at every info of that sink the module gets (the sink changes patch 0011 asks for,
  such as an analog jack switching its port from speakers to headphones), the sink's info
  is asked for without waiting, and the answer, on PulseAudio's thread, sets the value:
  true when the sink's active port is of type headphones or headset, or its
  device.form_factor is "headphone" or "headset"; false otherwise. The port's type is in
  PulseAudio's headers and library from 14.0 on (WebRTC's Debian bullseye sysroot has
  14.2); the library is loaded at run time and may be older, so the type is read only
  when the loaded library is 14 or newer, and the form factor alone decides otherwise.
  An answer about a sink the playout left, or one that comes after playout stopped,
  changes nothing. Two more symbols are loaded: pa_get_library_version and
  pa_proplist_gets.
- Windows Core Audio (AudioDeviceWindowsCore): at a start of playout, the render
  endpoint's form factor (PKEY_AudioEndpoint_FormFactor): Headphones or Headset is true,
  anything else or nothing false. It is read again when that endpoint says its form
  factor changed, and the value is false while the endpoint is not active (unplugged or
  disabled) and read again when it is active again. A change of the default output is
  not followed: the module's playout stays on the endpoint it was opened on (patch
  0015), and another device chosen starts playout again, which reads it.

Logged (info) when the value is set and what the system says is new, not again for a
sink's other changes (its volume):
  PulseAudio: playout on sink <name> (<index>), port <name or none> (type <number or
    unknown>), form factor <value or none>: sound to headphones yes|no
  PulseAudio: playout stopped: sound to headphones no
  Core Audio: playout on endpoint <name>, form factor <number> [(speakers|headphones|
    headset)] or unknown (playout started|form factor changed|endpoint active again):
    sound to headphones yes|no
  Core Audio: the playout's endpoint is not active (state <number>): sound to
    headphones no
  Core Audio: playout stopped: sound to headphones no

